/**
 * Cloudflare Workers config — the STAGING deploy of the built game (GS-staging).
 *
 * WHY THIS EXISTS AT ALL. Production stays on GitHub Pages at farcarry.vulpecula.games and must:
 * a PWA is bound to its ORIGIN, so every already-installed app is pinned there, and moving it would
 * mean every player uninstalling, reinstalling and hand-carrying their save across. Staging therefore
 * has to be a SEPARATE ORIGIN — `next.farcarry.vulpecula.games` — and not a path on the production
 * one, because `localStorage` is per-origin: a path would have staging and production sharing the
 * same `fc_*` save blobs, and a staging build with a bumped schema would write something production
 * refuses to read (`GS-save-integrity` would correctly drop that player into read-only mode).
 *
 * This is an ASSETS-ONLY Worker: there is no `main`, no server code, nothing to run. It exists to
 * serve `dist/` — which is one inlined index.html plus the PWA's install assets — at its own origin.
 *
 * `npx wrangler deploy` publishes the production branch; `npx wrangler versions upload` publishes a
 * preview URL per non-production branch, which is what gives a pull request something you can open on
 * a phone BEFORE it is merged. That is the part worth having: this whole file exists because a day of
 * play-test churn went straight to real users' installed app instead of to a link.
 */
{
  "$schema": "node_modules/wrangler/config-schema.json",
  "name": "far-carry-next",
  "compatibility_date": "2026-08-02",
  "assets": {
    "directory": "./dist",
    // The game has no client-side routing — every screen is a query param (`?screen=`), never a path
    // — so an unknown path is a genuine 404 and should say so. SPA-style rewriting would answer every
    // typo with a 200 and the game, which hides broken links rather than surfacing them.
    "not_found_handling": "none"
  },
  "observability": { "enabled": true }
}
